Table~\ref{tab:mosi} shows that no fusion style beats text alone on MOSI. With the style
chosen on held-out data, accuracy $H$ is $-0.62$ over twenty seeds (bootstrap $95\%$
interval $[-1.22,-0.07]$, which narrowly excludes zero, permutation $p=0.06$, $d_z=-0.47$); on MOSEI it is $+0.68$
($[+0.55,+0.82]$, $p<0.001$, $d_z=2.11$). Held-out data barely separate early from mid
fusion on either corpus (held-out accuracy $99.09$ vs.\ $99.11$ on MOSI, $71.31$ vs.\ 
$71.23$ on MOSEI); counted with the other style, $H$ is $-0.29$ ($p=0.22$) and $+0.37$
($p=0.001$). At five seeds, selecting hyper-parameters per configuration gave $-1.12$
and $+1.04$ (paired-$t$ $p=0.068$ and $0.057$; permutation $p=0.125$ for both). On MOSI the headroom is small and negative, and the bootstrap interval and the
permutation test disagree on whether it differs from zero; on MOSEI the gain is
measurable but below one point.

Selection matters. Late averaging posts the highest MOSEI test accuracy, $+1.43$ over
text, yet ranks last among the fusion styles on held-out accuracy ($65.05$). Choosing the
fusion style by its test mean would have reported a gain two to four times larger than
the ones the held-out data support.

The baseline matters here too. The best constant predictor scores $62.10$ accuracy on MOSI,
so audio-only and video-only both score \emph{below} a classifier that ignores its input.
MOSI's training majority is negative and its test majority positive, so a constant
predictor fit to the training split scores $37.90$: the same formula gives values $24$
points apart, depending on which $\pi_0$ is used.

\subsection{MELD with Frozen Encoders}\label{sec:meld}

The MELD rows of Table~\ref{tab:headroom} use the features released with that paper. We
therefore test how $H$ changes when the unimodal representation is strengthened using
frozen modern encoders, which MELD's public raw media allow. We re-extracted MELD with encoders that never saw a MELD label and were never
fine-tuned: BERT-base~\cite{devlin2019} on the official transcripts and
WavLM-base-plus~\cite{chen2022wavlm} on the audio of each clip, mean-pooled over the last
layer ($2$ of $13{,}708$ clips have no media). The protocol is that of the previous
subsection, training on the official training and development dialogues and testing on
the official test split. Text and audio are the modalities of the published rows.

